  "nonclaims": [
    "Validation is structural and the hygiene runner executes only the declared Python nodes. Rust arithmetic/parser tests and native guest transport checks require their separate Cargo commands.",
    "The fixture uses a separate integer row oracle for economic outcomes and independently assembles framing/statement bytes, but reuses existing state constructors and hash primitives. Five vectors do not prove universal runtime or parser refinement.",
    "The mutation ledger separately replays the declared source mutant against an archived subject; packet validation alone does not execute it.",
    "Native guest library tests exercise the exact stdin transport. Native compilation checks the guest entry, but neither executes zkVM abort/commit branches nor produces a measured guest or genuine receipt.",
    "The statement is only the inner economic payload. Complete CBC release/profile admission, authenticated subjects and grants, active policy membership, current store authority, durable publication and no-bypass remain open.",
    "No Lean, Kani, ESSO, heavy local proof build, live migration, activation or full formal-core/V3 completion is claimed."
  ]
